# NOTE: dist/ is intentionally committed (not ignored). This package is consumed as a git
# dependency, and enterprise npm setups often set `ignore-scripts=true`, which skips any
# build on install. Shipping a prebuilt dist/ makes the git dependency resolve
# unconditionally. Rebuild with `npm run build` and commit dist/ with the source change;
# CI's "dist/ is the build of src/" step rebuilds it from clean and fails if it differs.

# Written by test/parity/dump.test.ts on every run, for reading by eye.
